  ...
};
```
Hmm, but `global $x` needs to link to global. Since global vars live in a single map (per "global scope" — actually PHP globals are per-script-execution and shared), refs are shared_ptr<Value> pointing to the global map's values — unordered_map values are stable, so we can hold shared_ptr? No: map<string, Value> values are not shared_ptr; we can hold a pointer `Value*` — stable because unordered_map nodes are stable (except erasure). Alternatively store map<string, shared_ptr<Value>> so refs are shared_ptr<Value>. Simpler and uniform with array cells. Do that.

